From 8cb7d66c4e54222c1b8095b424ca84680ba066cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IMD Ember <operator@imdember.invalid>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:59:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] GOLD: credit top-ups at finality again (~15 min), gold
 "crediting" note meanwhile; exact smart-account effect

Owner decision after Swarm audit e4a57f91 (2026-10-27): GOLD spent before finality on a payment
that is later reorged out cannot be recovered off chain, so the browser no longer asks for fast
credit. A paid top-up is kept per wallet in this browser (pendingGoldCredit.ts) and shown in gold
as "+N crediting" next to the top bar's GOLD balance and on the purchase page, with the expected
time, until the ledger books it; the top bar reads the ledger every 30 s while one is pending.
The purchase page now states the 15-minute wait. The server route stays off (GOLD_FAST_CREDIT
unset); existing fast credits are all settled.

Also: a delegated receipt counts as the intended effect only when it holds exactly one event of
that kind for this sender from the intended contract (audit I-8), and the pending note takes the
payment's hash, not the approval's still shown while the payment is being sent.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
